{"title":"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2:_Mod_Arithmetic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2: Mod Arithmetic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(similar_to_[1])\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (similar to [1])</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown below, convex pentagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56ff6dcfd62e4e93c0469964d28b362ccff9c2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=3$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/457c786d44511f906a48d347140798f514c83311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=6$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93177aa484f3d901b77587ad2ed451dbb9d96b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=3$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566ac1c70b7e66e9f74957f36e5e9e3b72969d9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA=7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. The pentagon is originally positioned in the plane with vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> at the origin and vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis. The pentagon is then rolled clockwise to the right along the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis. Which side will touch the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4ede76a20da0615982f01248525595f42229d075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2009$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" /> on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6ac5c8a85c125cb27930bfe3c7aa4b9cd98e12.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(3mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt)); dotfactor=4;  pair A=(0,0), Ep=7*dir(105), B=3*dir(0); pair D=Ep+B; pair C=intersectionpoints(Circle(D,6),Circle(B,4))[1]; pair[] ds={A,B,C,D,Ep};  dot(ds); draw(B--C--D--Ep--A); draw((6,6)..(8,4)..(8,3),EndArrow(3)); xaxis(&quot;$x$&quot;,-8,14,EndArrow(3));  label(&quot;$E$&quot;,Ep,NW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$(0,0)=A$&quot;,A,SW);  label(&quot;$3$&quot;,midpoint(A--B),N); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,midpoint(B--C),NW); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,midpoint(C--D),NE); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,midpoint(D--Ep),S); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,midpoint(Ep--A),W); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"238\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769bbc4eadbaede70c82a88ef9c61f6e4b022fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } \\overline{AB} \\qquad \\text{(B) } \\overline{BC} \\qquad \\text{(C) } \\overline{CD} \\qquad \\text{(D) } \\overline{DE} \\qquad \\text{(E) } \\overline{EA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"431\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter of the polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89cf1eb8cff0522187b8b774ac5f4a252515d310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+4+6+3+7 = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" />. Hence as we roll the polygon to the right, every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> will be the bottom side.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c7b2fc8432f0b11697c1bd25d9f880673b00bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2009 = 23 \\times 87 + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"14\" />. Thus at some point in time we will get the situation when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d170a60530295d34be30512534fa1fcee6b659a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(2001,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is the bottom side. Obviously, at this moment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/3/333f93e180d11b2368c1f415ab21d4c145b933d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(2004,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>After that, the polygon rotates around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> until point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> hits the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaab62cb65e46d295bb696045601ebdf218de7f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2008,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>And finally, the polygon rotates around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> until point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> hits the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> axis at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2346b93152c0f32e75643d01acd706f59e8adc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2014,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\nAt this point the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f0f80faa2ebb109d0e109182a72d0be3550e0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\overline{CD}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"27\" /> touches the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f89123ebb1e348ad7f3e651fb400dd2cc068b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2009,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2:_Mod_Arithmetic\">Solution 2: Mod Arithmetic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2: Mod Arithmetic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c4fb6aa61fa922a943b3a97016f19b4e68e30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2009\\equiv8($\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/673f176b6acea1c48c6ff4a9d73aa452fa2db11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" />, so it will end up on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> + a total of 8 more units. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/9170b77a2a79f744b5dabf67908e5ec47f359d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4&lt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf698bf5820c63a00bd7cc91b71c79a470d27c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+6=10&gt;8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"14\" />, so it ends on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> for an answer of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28similar_to_.5B1.5D.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(similar_to_[1])\">Solution 3 (similar to [1])</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (similar to [1])\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The acquired distance per a revolution among the centre of the pentagon considers 23 units from position <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/634e0b5a38397ec12d800d3e42721bd8d8be2c9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2009 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/2/43237f2818ad6cfd23d130cde3268099dc02e3b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{quo}(2009,23) = 87$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eef8449f81475a1027adbef8fbbd342d27cd35f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$87 \\cdot 23 = 2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> slots are covered continuously before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is positioned on the lefthand vertex once more, particularly, at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809dc7fcef46e9521d47a4863c44165119a6e3d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2001,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdd250944bdcc8b36b68cc80ff4bce58acd2189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(2004,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> so in a rotation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c0326236e38ec964d2da9081d0bba7755594ad2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(2008,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fc6c6fe1b678ddec69c04f3c0b030a3282f3d81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"25\" /> has the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f89123ebb1e348ad7f3e651fb400dd2cc068b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2009,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B\">2009 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title